sers/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"unlabeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-03-22T21:13:34Z","label":{"name":"requires triage","color":"ffff00"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":6286831951,"node_id":"MIE_lADOCX5JB85GKvvPzwAAAAF2uXFP","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/6286831951","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"milestoned","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-03-22T21:13:38Z","milestone":{"title":"1.4.x"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":6286832506,"node_id":"LE_lADOCX5JB85GKvvPzwAAAAF2uXN6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/6286832506","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-03-22T21:13:43Z","label":{"name":"question","color":"d876e3"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1075648171","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7842#issuecomment-1075648171","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7842","id":1075648171,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB85AHRar","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-03-22T21:16:57Z","updated_at":"2022-03-22T21:16:57Z","body":"your mapping requires that the primary key be established to include \"id\" and \"parent\" explicitly:\r\n\r\n```py\r\nclass NodeRel(Base):\r\n    table = select(\r\n        Node.id,\r\n        Node.parent,\r\n        literal(0).label('depth')).cte(recursive=True)\r\n    __table__ = table.union_all(select(\r\n        Node.id,\r\n        table.c.parent,\r\n        table.c.depth + literal(1),\r\n        ).select_from(Node).join(table, Node.parent == table.c.id))\r\n\r\n    __mapper_args__ = {\r\n        \"primary_key\": (__table__.c.id, __table__.c.parent)\r\n    }\r\n    def __repr__(self):\r\n        return f'<NodeRel {self.parent} -> {self.id}>'\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\notherwise, when you ask for \"id=4\", it gets all rows with \"id=4\" and as far as the ORM knows, \"id\" is the only column that's a primary key.\r\n\r\nHowever, the above mapping has a totally separate problem in that the ORM is attempting to \"reduce\" the columns given for that primary key to columns that are known to have unique values; columns that are equated to each other are assumed to have the same value and are reduced.  So the above \"primary_key\" argument will be silently truncated back down to the \"id\" column alone. \r\n\r\nat the moment, the only workaround I have is to patch away the function in question:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/mapper.py b/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/mapper.py\r\nindex 967c1064ad..7fe7716194 100644\r\n--- a/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/mapper.py\r\n+++ b/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/mapper.py\r\n@@ -1347,6 +1347,7 @@ class Mapper(\r\n                     self._pks_by_table[k.table] = util.OrderedSet()\r\n                 self._pks_by_table[k.table].add(k)\r\n \r\n+\r\n         # otherwise, see that we got a full PK for the mapped table\r\n         elif (\r\n             self.persist_selectable not in self._pks_by_table\r\n@@ -1379,13 +1380,10 @@ class Mapper(\r\n             # determine primary key from argument or persist_selectable pks -\r\n             # reduce to the minimal set of columns\r\n             if self._primary_key_argument:\r\n-                primary_key = sql_util.reduce_columns(\r\n-                    [\r\n+                primary_key =[\r\n                         self.persist_selectable.corresponding_column(c)\r\n                         for c in self._primary_key_argument\r\n-                    ],\r\n-                    ignore_nonexistent_tables=True,\r\n-                )\r\n+                    ]\r\n             else:\r\n                 primary_key = sql_util.reduce_columns(\r\n                     self._pks_by_table[self.persist_selectable],\r\n```\r\n\r\nthe the rows are identified as individual primary keys:\r\n\r\n```\r\nWITH RECURSIVE anon_1(id, parent, depth) AS \r\n(SELECT nodes.id AS id, nodes.parent AS parent, ? AS depth \r\nFROM nodes UNION ALL SELECT nodes.id AS id, anon_1.parent AS parent, anon_1.depth + ? AS anon_2 \r\nFROM nodes JOIN anon_1 ON nodes.parent = anon_1.id)\r\n SELECT anon_1.id, anon_1.parent, anon_1.depth \r\nFROM anon_1 \r\nWHERE anon_1.id = ?\r\n2022-03-22 17:16:33,295 INFO sqlalchemy.engine.Engine [generated in 0.00014s] (0, 1, 4)\r\n2022-03-22 17:16:33,295 DEBUG sqlalchemy.engine.Engine Col ('id', 'parent', 'depth')\r\n2022-03-22 17:16:33,295 DEBUG sqlalchemy.engine.Engine Row (4, 3, 0)\r\n2022-03-22 17:16:33,295 DEBUG sqlalchemy.engine.Engine Row (4, 2, 1)\r\n2022-03-22 17:16:33,295 DEBUG sqlalchemy.engine.Engine Row (4, 1, 2)\r\n2022-03-22 17:16:33,295 DEBUG sqlalchemy.engine.Engine Row (4, None, 3)\r\n<NodeRel 3 -> 4>\r\n<NodeRel 2 -> 4>\r\n<NodeRel 1 -> 4>\r\n<NodeRel None -> 4>\r\n\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1075648171/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":6286852821,"node_id":"RTE_lADOCX5JB85GKvvPzwAAAAF2ucLV","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/6286852821","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"renamed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-03-22T21:17:14Z","rename":{"from":"Problem creating a mapper with a recursive CTE as a __table__","to":"primary key reduction logic tripped up by recursive CTE"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1075659563","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7842#issuecomment-1075659563","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7842","id":1075659563,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB85AHUMr","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-03-22T21:25:14Z","updated_at":"2022-03-22T21:25:14Z","body":"it's because Node.parent is a foreign key to Node.id, so the ORM assumes these will always be equal.  it doesnt see that there's a UNION in there redefining the value of the column down below.  \r\n\r\nSo you can work around this by using a name-only column that isn't related to \"parent\" like this:\r\n\r\n```py\r\nclass NodeRel(Base):\r\n    table = select(\r\n        Node.id,\r\n        column(\"parent\"), #Node.parent,\r\n        literal(0).label('depth')).cte(recursive=True)\r\n    __table__ = table.union_all(select(\r\n        Node.id,\r\n        table.c.parent,\r\n        table.c.depth + literal(1),\r\n        ).select_from(Node).join(table, Node.parent == table.c.id))\r\n\r\n    __mapper_args__ = {\r\n        \"primary_key\": (__table__.c.id, __table__.c.parent)\r\n    }\r\n    def __repr__(self):\r\n        return f'<NodeRel {self.parent} -> {self.id}>'\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nthen it sees both cols as uniquely part of the PK.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1075659563/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.