","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1075774251/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"sqla-tester","id":8250554,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyNTA1NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8250554?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester","html_url":"https://github.com/sqla-tester","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqla-tester/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1075775449","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7842#issuecomment-1075775449","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7842","id":1075775449,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB85AHwfZ","user":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-03-23T00:17:07Z","updated_at":"2022-03-23T00:17:07Z","body":"going to see if we can remove that \"reduction\" logic for the case of user-defined PK.   This should be safe for 1.4, there's a slight chance it might change the structure of an existing mapper PK definition that is badly defined but such a mapping should still function.  ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1075775449/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1075985437","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7842#issuecomment-1075985437","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/7842","id":1075985437,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB85AIjwd","user":{"login":"K1DV5","id":40162008,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTYyMDA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40162008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5","html_url":"https://github.com/K1DV5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-03-23T06:50:36Z","updated_at":"2022-03-23T06:50:36Z","body":"> it's because Node.parent is a foreign key to Node.id, so the ORM assumes these will always be equal. it doesnt see that there's a UNION in there redefining the value of the column down below.\r\n> \r\n> So you can work around this by using a name-only column that isn't related to \"parent\" like this:\r\n> \r\n> ```python\r\n> class NodeRel(Base):\r\n>     table = select(\r\n>         Node.id,\r\n>         column(\"parent\"), #Node.parent,\r\n>         literal(0).label('depth')).cte(recursive=True)\r\n>     __table__ = table.union_all(select(\r\n>         Node.id,\r\n>         table.c.parent,\r\n>         table.c.depth + literal(1),\r\n>         ).select_from(Node).join(table, Node.parent == table.c.id))\r\n> \r\n>     __mapper_args__ = {\r\n>         \"primary_key\": (__table__.c.id, __table__.c.parent)\r\n>     }\r\n>     def __repr__(self):\r\n>         return f'<NodeRel {self.parent} -> {self.id}>'\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> then it sees both cols as uniquely part of the PK.\r\n\r\nThis worked. Thanks! Will close the issue when it is fixed internally.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1075985437/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"K1DV5","id":40162008,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTYyMDA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40162008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5","html_url":"https://github.com/K1DV5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/K1DV5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":6293084824,"node_id":"LE_lADOCX5JB85GKvvPzwAAAAF3GNqY","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/6293084824","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","